Here is the commit message:
Check if player is in arena on food level change.

This commit fixes a bug.

During a food level change event, if the arena is running and the food level lock is enabled, we just need to also make sure that the given player is actually in the arena, otherwise it affects everyone on the server.

Here is the root cause:
The food level change event handler only checked whether the arena was running and whether food level locking (`lockFoodLevel`) was enabled, but failed to verify that the specific player triggering the event was actually inside the arena (`arena.inArena(p)`). Since this listener presumably applies globally across the server, any player's food level change event—even those not participating in the arena—would be cancelled as long as some arena was running and had food level locking enabled. This caused an unintended side effect where players outside the arena had their hunger/food level changes blocked, which is an overly broad application of a game mechanic that should only apply to arena participants.

Here is the patch:

     public void onFoodLevelChange(FoodLevelChangeEvent event) {
         if (!(event.getEntity() instanceof Player)) {
             return;
         }

         Player p = (Player) event.getEntity();

         if (arena.isRunning()) {
-            if (lockFoodLevel) {
+            if (arena.inArena(p) && lockFoodLevel) {
                 event.setCancelled(true);
             }
         } else {
             // Always locked in lobby/spec
             if (arena.inLobby(p) || arena.inSpec(p)) {
                 event.setCancelled(true);
             }
         }
     }



