if (lockFoodLevel) {
Reason: The handler cancels the food level change event solely based on whether the arena is running and whether `lockFoodLevel` is enabled, without checking if the specific player (`p`) triggering the event is actually inside the arena. Since this event listener is global, it incorrectly cancels food level changes for all players on the server whenever any arena is running with food locking enabled, not just the players participating in that arena.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (arena.inArena(p) && lockFoodLevel) {
Reason: By adding the `arena.inArena(p)` check, the event cancellation now only applies to players who are actually inside the arena. This ensures the food level lock mechanic is scoped correctly to arena participants, preventing unintended side effects on players outside the arena.

